 Time Drama However, the match was far from over. Santiago Rodriguez , who had come on as a substitute, sparked a late revival for Botafogo . In the 85th minute, he pulled one back to give the home fans a glimmer of hope. The atmosphere shifted instantly as the hosts threw men forward in a desperate attempt to salvage a point. In the second minute of stoppage time, the tension reached a breaking point. Danilo found Santiago Rodriguez once again, and the forward clinicaly converted to make it 3-2. The final minutes were played at a frantic pace, but the referee's final whistle at 90+6' brought the comeback attempt to a halt. Athletico Paranaense escaped with all three points after a resilient defensive stand in the dying moments."
